    {
      "GroupDto": {
        "GroupName": "T0H1N1B11",
        "Description": "NAND reading (inputs A and B, BIAS constantly on, threshold 0.125) of the shipped \u0027Logic Gate NOT-NAND\u0027 gate. Role in the 4-bit adder: first XOR stage of stage 0\u0027s partial sum (chain 11 of 13), Y = NAND(A0, B0), feeding T0H1N311.A. The whole 4-bit adder composes at the logic layer, not optically: every gate\u0027s truth table is extracted once in isolation, so each stage restores clean 0/1 levels by construction \u2014 there is deliberately no multi-stage passive optical cascade here. The fan-out of the A, B and Cin bits onto several gates happens at the logic layer (each gate input is driven by the same network bit); shared stages \u2014 and each stage\u0027s carry-out, which must reach the next stage\u0027s several carry-in pins \u2014 are duplicated as extra gate instances because the canvas wires one waveguide per pin (like NAND1A/NAND1B in \u0027Logic Gate Half Adder\u0027).",
        "Identifier": "group_4e5a504dc1e3420ea329e426d1a47d77",
        "IdGuid": "1a9bd1fc-ada2-41a4-a90e-9f016dbe983e",
